        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Extract Account Info"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1769751973741"
          },
          "code": "EXTRACT_ACCOUNT_INFO",
          "id": "1773142650738",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1773142650739_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are an information extractor for text parsed from United States bank documents (for example: check images, direct deposit forms, voided checks, bank letters, account verification forms).\n\nInputs:\n{{$context.$variables.attachmentRawContent}}\n{{$context.$system.$inputMessage}} \n\nTask:\nExtract only these fields:\n- AccountNumber\n- RoutingNumber\n- BankName\n- BranchName\n- AccountType\n\nCore behavior:\n- Use both labeled cues and unlabeled document patterns common in US bank documents.\n- Do not guess or invent values.\n- If a value is missing, blank, placeholder-like, or not confidently extractable, return NOT_FOUND.\n- Return only the requested structured output.\n\nExtraction strategy (important):\n1) RoutingNumber\n- Must be exactly 9 digits (ABA).\n- Prefer explicit labels when present (Routing, ABA, RTN, Transit).\n- If labels are absent, infer from common US check patterns:\n  - MICR line usually has routing first, then account number.\n  - Routing is the 9-digit candidate that best fits check/direct-deposit context.\n- Reject non-routing 9-digit numbers when context indicates other IDs (tax ID, reference, check number).\n- If uncertain, return NOT_FOUND.\n\n2) AccountNumber\n- Treat as text only.\n- Never cast to numeric type; never scientific notation.\n- Prefer labels if present (Account Number, Acct, A/C).\n- If labels are absent, infer from common patterns:\n  - On checks, account number is often in MICR line near routing number.\n  - On direct-deposit forms, account number is typically the longer numeric banking identifier associated with routing.\n- Valid account candidate rules:\n  - Must contain at least one digit in original span.\n  - After removing spaces/hyphens, must be digits only, length 4-17.\n  - Preserve leading zeros.\n- Critical blank handling:\n  - If the extracted span is only punctuation/delimiters/wrappers/whitespace, return NOT_FOUND.\n  - Do NOT return delimiter shells such as \"-: :-\", \"-:    :-\", \": :\", \"--\", \"()\", \"[]\", \"{}\".\n  - Do NOT return placeholder tokens: N/A, NA, NULL, NONE, TBD, UNKNOWN.\n- If candidate conflicts with routing number or looks like check/reference number, reject it.\n- If uncertain, return NOT_FOUND.\n\n3) BankName\n- Extract if clearly identifiable from document header/body/check imprint context.\n- If unclear, return NOT_FOUND.\n\n4) BranchName\n- Extract only when clearly stated/implied as branch/location.\n- If unclear, return NOT_FOUND.\n\n5) AccountType\n- Extract only if clearly indicated (Checking, Savings, etc.).\n- If unclear, return NOT_FOUND.\n\nConfidence policy:\n- Prefer NOT_FOUND over weak guesses.\n- If multiple candidates exist, choose the one best supported by US check/direct-deposit structure and nearby context.\n\nOutput format:\nReturn JSON object with exactly these string fields:\n{\n  \"AccountNumber\": \"...\",\n  \"RoutingNumber\": \"...\",\n  \"BankName\": \"...\",\n  \"BranchName\": \"...\",\n  \"AccountType\": \"...\"\n}\n- Every value must be a JSON string.\n- No extra keys, no explanation text."
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n    \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n    \"type\": \"object\",\n    \"properties\": {\n        \"BranchName\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"BankName\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"RoutingNumber\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"AccountType\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"AccountNumber\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        }\n    }\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
